<!-- SECTION 4: WHO CAN FILE -->
<section class="content-section" id="who-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="text-content">
            <h2 class="section-title">When Mumbai Taxpayers Receive Section 156 Demands</h2>
            <div class="content-text">
                
                <p><strong>Salaried individuals at BKC/Nariman Point/Lower Parel</strong> &ndash; Most common: CPC Section 143(1) mismatch. TDS credit not given (employer delayed deposit, wrong PAN, bank TDS missing). Deductions rejected (wrong section code). Patron reconciles all TDS sources and files rectification.</p>
                <p><strong>Business owners at Fort/Dadar/Andheri</strong> &ndash; After scrutiny (Section 143(3)): expenses disallowed, unexplained credits (Section 68), income reclassified. Demand includes additional tax + interest + penalty. Patron represents before AO and manages demand response.</p>
                <p><strong>Powai/Andheri startup founders</strong> &ndash; ESOP taxation disputes, angel tax (Section 56(2)(viib)), capital gains, advance tax demands (Section 210(3)). Patron handles startup-specific demand responses.</p>
                <p><strong>NRIs with Mumbai property</strong> &ndash; Capital gains from property sale, rental income, deemed income. NRIs often don't check Indian e-filing portal &ndash; demands become final. Patron provides NRI demand monitoring service.</p>
                <p><strong>Mumbai companies</strong> &ndash; Transfer pricing adjustments (BKC MNC subsidiaries), depreciation disallowance, Section 80 deduction rejection, penalty for misreporting. Corporate demands can run into crores. For <a href="/private-limited-company-compliance">Pvt Ltd Compliance</a>, see our page.</p>
                <p><strong>TDS/TCS deductors</strong> &ndash; Section 200A(1) for TDS short deduction, late filing interest (Section 234E), processing mismatches. Section 206CB(1) for TCS non-collection. Patron manages TDS/TCS demand responses.</p>

            </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

